          "description": {
            "comment": "The garden warbler (Sylvia borin) is songbird, and one of the most studied for it migratory behavior between its breeding grounds in Europe to its wintering grounds in central Africa. During migration, they can metabolize up to 19% of their breast muscle and 39% of their digestive tract. They also have a rich diverse song. This sample was collected by Julia Slezacek of a female from Ponza Island, Italy, and procured for studies on migration by Silvia Fuselli, Steve Smith, and Leonida Fusani, to generate a chromosome level reference assembly as part of the G10K-VGP Project.",
